# ⚠ The jet ratio is only meaningful against its OWN fixture. `ray_capsule`
# fires _bray, which runs down the capsule axis and lands on a cap; jet_capsule
# fires the diagonal _bray_d, which lands on the barrel -- a 515 ns row and a
# 968 ns row for the same function. Dividing one by the other would have
# reported the jet at 2.6x when it is 1.38x. Every jet added in 2.10.1 has a
# primal row at the same fixture, which is what makes the ratio readable off the
# CSV rather than assembled by hand from two different geometries.
# [measured: bench-history.csv ray_capsule_diag]
