# ================================================================
# 3.3.6 -- the modules and paths no row reached (roadmap D114, D115, D044)
# ================================================================
# ⛔ Through 3.3.5, 11 of the 35 modules had no row and the bench called none of
# linalg_ext's or f64_util's functions, so the LM / L-BFGS allocation hoists and
# calc_ext's costs had no number (D114); the 3.3.0 number-theory repairs and the
# 3.3.5 repairs were timed only in scratch harnesses (D115); and gjk_epa_3d /
# mpr_penetration had no separated-pair row and time_of_impact no row (D044).
# [measured: docs/audit/2026-09-30-deferment-audit.md D114, D115, D044; includes above]
#
# Every row below is REGISTERED LAST (see main) for the heap-shift reason documented
# above the jac_rev pair, and uses `bench` so lib/bench.cyr sizes its windows for the
# resolution bar.
# ⚠ EACH ROW RETURNS WHAT DECIDES ITS PATH -- a Result tag, a verdict, an exact
# value -- and _b6_setup checks every one once before any row is timed, refusing to
# run them when one is off. A row that silently timed an Err, a fallback or the
# other branch would report a cost for code it never ran; the jac_rev and CGA rows
# above carry the same guard.
var _B6_FAIL = 0;

fn _b6_check(ok, name) {
    if (ok == 1) { return 0; }
    syscall(1, 1, "FATAL: 3.3.6 row ", 17);
    syscall(1, 1, name, strlen(name));
    println(" does not take the path its name says");
    _B6_FAIL = _B6_FAIL + 1;
    return 1;
}

fn _b6_q(a, b) { return f64_div(f64_from(a), f64_from(b)); }

